      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, because getIpConfigurationForCallback is always called with the interface name. If you configured it using the mac address, `mIpConfigurations.get(identifier);` will return null.\n\nI am not entirely sure what the best solution here is. The fact that server mode interfaces are not tracked by the EthernetNetworkFactory (which is really a bug we need to address at some point) makes this much more annoying; otherwise, you could just start querying the factory for IpConfiguration and capabilities.\n\nContrary to what I wrote below, I think you probably want to add a getIpConfiguration() and a getNetworkCapabilities() function. Both do the look up by iface name, then MAC, then return the default. You can retrieve the mac address via EthernetNetworkFactory (needs a getter) and store the mac address of the server mode interface (mTetheringInterface) in a member of EthernetTracker (mTetheringInterfaceMac or something). That\u0027s not terrible, but maybe you have a better idea?\n\nIf you decide to go with above approach, you might want to split these changes into a few CLs to make review easier. I.e. start tracking the mac address for mTetheringInterface, add getters for the mac to the factory, add getIpConfiguration(), and getNetworkCapabilities().",
